      "content": "Here's a breakdown of the specific changes I made:\n\n* \"Customer: yo\" became \"'I've been trying to obtain my refund'\": I changed \"yo\" to a more formal greeting, as it's not suitable for official documents. This is because \"yo\" can come across as too casual and informal.\n* \"i been tryin\" became \"'I've been trying'\": The contraction \"I've been trying\" is a standard way to express the need to have been in the process of trying something. The original text used a colloquialism \"bein',\" which is not typically used in formal writing.\n* \"ain't\" became \"aren't\": This change emphasizes that the speaker is actually experiencing frustration and disappointment rather than simply stating something as fact.\n* \"gonna\" became \"will\": \"Gonna\" is an informal contraction of \"going to.\" In formal writing, we typically use the full phrase \"will\" to convey the same meaning.\n* \"right now\" became \":as soon as possible\" or similar: While \"right now\" can be used informally, in professional writing, it's more common to use phrases like \"as soon as possible\" to convey a similar sense of urgency.",
